  "result": "**What it does:** Order utilities for a shop backend — `calcTotal` sums item price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies coupon codes, `averageItemPrice`, and `formatOrder` renders an order with discounted total.\n\n**Bugs:**\n1. `calcTotal:5` — `i <= items.length` overruns by one; last iteration reads `items[length]` (undefined) → `TypeError`. Use `i < items.length`.\n2. `averageItemPrice:20` — divides by `items.length` with no empty-array guard → `NaN` (0/0) on empty input.\n3. `formatOrder:23`/`calcTotal` — no guarding of missing `items`/fields; e.g. an order with no `items` throws. Minor vs. #1 but worth a guard.\n\n#1 is the critical one — every `calcTotal` call currently crashes.",
